{"term":"tortoise","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:ea9a87787771b16dbc","definition":"Any of various land-dwelling reptiles, of the family Testudinidae (chiefly Canada, US) or the order Testudines (chiefly UK, Australia, New Zealand, Ireland, South Africa, India), whose body is enclosed in a shell (carapace plus plastron). The animal can withdraw its head and four legs partially into the shell, providing some protection from predators.","example":"The tortoise, with its characteristic protrusion of the head and neck, was a symbol sacred to Venus. It represented the procreative principle.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["shellpad"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["African spurred tortoise","Aldabra giant tortoise","angonoka tortoise","Bolson tortoise","boofhead tortoise","Burmese star tortoise","Charles Island giant tortoise","desert tortoise","elephantine tortoise","Floreana giant tortoise","Galápagos giant tortoise","Galapagos giant tortoise","Galapagos tortoise","Galápagos tortoise","geometric tortoise","giant tortoise","golden tortoise beetle","gopher tortoise","Hermann's tortoise","hinge-back tortoise","hinged-back tortoise","hinged tortoise","Horsfield's tortoise","Indian star tortoise","leopard tortoise","Madagascar tortoise","pancake tortoise","ploughshare tortoise","radiated tortoise","red-footed tortoise"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tortoise#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:b10c6a9423551571ed","definition":"Synonym of cat (sense 11, a wheeled shelter)","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":["cat"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["African spurred tortoise","Aldabra giant tortoise","angonoka tortoise","Bolson tortoise","boofhead tortoise","Burmese star tortoise","Charles Island giant tortoise","desert tortoise","elephantine tortoise","Floreana giant tortoise","Galápagos gian